          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "Enjoy a half-day city tour, exploring the rich history and cultural treasures of Cusco, the former capital of the Inca Empire. Your first stop will be the Qorikancha Temple (Temple of the Sun), once the most important religious site in the Inca Empire, renowned for its incredible gold-covered walls and its connection to the sun god, Inti.\n\nContinue to the Cusco Cathedral, an impressive colonial structure located in the Plaza de Armas. The cathedral is home to remarkable religious artwork and showcases a blend of Spanish and Incan architectural styles. \n\nExplore nearby archaeological sites such as Sacsayhuamán, an ancient Inca fortress with massive, precisely cut stones that fit together without mortar. Then, visit Qenqo, a ceremonial site that was likely used for astronomical observations and rituals. Finally, stop at Tambomachay, an Incan site known for its water fountains and its connection to water worship. "
    },
