    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:49b18e3fb3f9ec7b",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9631674f1ee347a2e2ba7062f268c34cfdad40e131e118ea650eeec39019cfed",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1IJ-ifZl_wfTwk-xMrqNJcO6OBMQunbcA",
        "documentSha256": "e72781a19f85cef319201422e08f82b1f3826c037805c98f97b2081b4eed559c",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0053",
            "textSha256": "8bae982fbe977b29e4fcea9d9742bf60fc38086bfb35cc258138703ae8ed6afd"
          },
          {
            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0054",
            "textSha256": "4a3221553f51a9795b8b6be7486e5e2bde98343353d9b3af5f1b2d1818fe40f6"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "Embark on a fascinating full-day tour to explore the incredible sites of Maras, Moray, and the Salineras. Start with a visit to Moray, an ancient Incan agricultural site famous for its impressive circular terraces. These concentric terraces were used by the Incas for experimental farming, allowing them to study how different crops thrived in various microclimates.\n\nContinue to the village of Maras, where you will explore the Salineras, the ancient salt mines still in use today. These salt pans, located on the slopes of a mountain, have been in operation since Inca times. You’ll learn about the traditional methods of salt extraction and see the vast, white terraces where salt is harvested from the natural spring water. Overnight at Sacred Valley. "
    },
